{
  "moduleId": "m00337",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00337:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Carbohydrate Biosynthesis: Gluconeogenesis"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "fbd831be-1be6-4733-b788-d8323f5be1b3"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "(S)-lactate, alanine and glycerol are oxidized to pyruvate. Pyruvate then undergoes gluconeogenesis to form glucose."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00337:caption:fig-00002-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The first seven-step biosynthesis of glucose from pyruvate via oxaloacetate, phosphoenolpyruvate, 2-phosphoglycerate, 3-phosphoglycerate, 1,3-bis-phosphoglycerate, glyceraldehyde, and dihydroxyacetone phosphate intermediates."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00337:caption:fig-00003-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "The remaining four steps of the biosynthesis of glucose from dihydroxyacetone phosphate, fructose 6-phosphate, and  glucose 6-phosphate intermediates."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Step 1 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Carboxylation"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": null,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "N-Carboxy biotin mediated pyruvate carboxylation leads to an intermediate, which is protonated to form oxaloacetate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_002.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 2 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Decarboxylation and Phosphorylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Magnesium-mediated phosphorylation of oxaloacetate with guanosine triphosphate yielded phosphoenolpyruvate, carbon dioxide, and guanosine diphosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Steps 3–4 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Hydration and Isomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "The hydration of phosphoenol pyruvate provided 2-phosphoglycerate that is phosphorated to yield  2,3-bisphosphoglycerate, which was then further hydrolyzed to form 3-phosphoglycerate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00005",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00005-title",
            "text": "Steps 5–7 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Phosphorylation, Reduction, and Tautomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "3-Phosphoglycerate is converted to dihydroxyacetone phosphate via  1,3-bisphosphoglycerate, an enzyme-bound thioester, and glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate intermediates."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00006",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00006-title",
            "text": "Step 8 of [[xref:fig-00003]]: Aldol Reaction"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "Deprotonation of an enzyme-bound iminium ion condenses with  glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate which upon isomerization providee fructose-1,6-bisphosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00007",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00007-title",
            "text": "Steps 9–10 of [[xref:fig-00003]]: Hydrolysis and Isomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00010"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00009",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00009-alt",
                  "text": "The phosphate hydrolysis of fructose-1,6-bisphosphate yields  fructose-6-phosphate  which isomerizes to glucose-6-phosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_009.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00008",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00337:title:sect-00008-title",
            "text": "Step 11 of [[xref:fig-00003]]: Hydrolysis"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00011",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00011"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00012",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00012"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00010",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00010-alt",
                  "text": "Enzymatic catalyzed dephosphorylation of glucose 6-phosphate to provide glucose and the phosphorylated enzyme."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_010.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00013",
              "segmentId": "m00337:para:para-00013"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00011",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00337:alt:fig-00011-alt",
                  "text": "Pyruvate reacts with adenosine triphosphate, nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride, hydronium ion, and guanosine triphosphate to form glucose, adenosine diphosphate, nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide cation, guanosine diphosphate, and phosphate ion."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_08_011.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
